content.text:
Our JS options merger corrupts the shared defaults object. Save /workspace/options.mjs:

const DEFAULTS = {
  retries: 3,
  timeoutMs: 5000,
  headers: { accept: "application/json" },
};

export function withDefaults(opts = {}) {
  return Object.assign(DEFAULTS, opts);
}

export function getDefaults() { return DEFAULTS; }

Object.assign mutates its FIRST argument, so every call permanently rewrites DEFAULTS for the whole process. Write options.test.mjs (node:test) before fixing: call withDefaults({retries: 0}), then withDefaults({}) and assert retries is back to 3; also assert getDefaults().retries === 3 afterward, and that mutating result.headers.accept on a returned object does not change DEFAULTS.headers.accept. Run node --test, watch it fail, then fix with a non-mutating merge (fresh object each call, headers cloned and merged one level down). Rerun green and add a test that unknown extra keys survive the merge.

tools_list = await mcp.list_tools("tools")
for t in tools_list:
    print(t["name"], t["inputSchema"])

